#   🚀 Building Secure Enterprise Network Architecture on Azure with Terraform

Over the past week, I designed and deployed a segmented enterprise infrastructure for Aurum Manufacturing Group using Terraform and Microsoft Azure. This project was more than just provisioning resources, it was about applying real-world security architecture principles in the cloud.

#   🔑 Key Achievements

-   Hub-and-Spoke Virtual Network Design: Centralized control with clear segmentation for users, admins, guests, and DMZ workloads.

#   Network Segmentation & Zero Trust:

- DMZ for public-facing services (Linux web server running Flask).

    - Internal subnet hosting Active Directory Domain Services (Windows Server).

    - Guest subnet isolated from core infrastructure.

- Secure Remote Access: Implemented Azure Bastion to eliminate direct public RDP/SSH exposure.

- Traffic Control & Inspection:

    - Azure Firewall with custom rule collections.

    - Route tables directing all outbound traffic through the firewall.

- Centralized Monitoring: Integrated Log Analytics Workspace for diagnostics, firewall logs, and visibility into network activity.

- Infrastructure as Code: Entire environment provisioned and managed via Terraform, ensuring repeatability and automation.


#   🛡️ Security Focus

- Adopted a Zero Trust model — every subnet and workload is isolated and explicitly allowed only what it needs.

- Applied least privilege principles to network flows.

- Built a secure DMZ that inspects and controls traffic before it reaches internal systems.

#   🌍 Why This Matters

This project simulates a real-world enterprise environment where cloud networking, security, and automation converge. It demonstrates how organizations can:

    - Modernize infrastructure with Terraform automation.

    - Strengthen defenses with Azure-native security controls.

    - Achieve visibility and compliance through centralized logging.

#   Outcome

A resilient, secure, and automated enterprise network — a blueprint for organizations looking to embrace cloud infrastructure while maintaining strong security posture.

